Falsifies `credential_protocol::proofs::a_request_word_round_trips_every_field`.

The defect: the identity length is read one bit low, `w0 >> 15` where the encoder shifts by 16.
This is the defect this harness can catch, and the choice is deliberate: its own doc comment
records that a swap applied to BOTH sides leaves it verifying, because an encoder round-tripped
through its own decoder moves with the defect. A one-sided shift does not move together, which
is the shape this harness is actually evidence for.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(id_len(w) == i)`, at any identity length with a bit
above the lowest set, where a server parses a length the client never sent and reads the wrong
run of bytes out of the shared page.

diff --git a/crates/credential_protocol/src/lib.rs b/crates/credential_protocol/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/credential_protocol/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/credential_protocol/src/lib.rs
@@ -242,3 +242,3 @@ pub const fn operation(w0: u64) -> u64 {
 pub const fn id_len(w0: u64) -> usize {
-    ((w0 >> 16) & 0xffff) as usize
+    ((w0 >> 15) & 0xffff) as usize
 }
